course: dictionary
lesson: 9968
title: Teach: helping someone learn
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Teach is a verb, and its past form is taught. To teach means to help someone learn something by showing or explaining it. «In the old days poor children were taught to call richer people sir» shows children being shown how to speak, so taught means they learned it from others.
explain: Teach can also mean giving lessons as a job, and a lesson can be something you learn from an experience. «That will teach you to leave your bike outside!» means you have learned the hard way. Nobody had to explain it to you: the mistake taught the lesson.
explain: A good check is to swap in a different word. Taught can often be replaced by showed or explained, so try those in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Teach means to help someone learn something by showing or explaining it.
fact: The past tense of teach is taught: «Jesus taught the Golden Rule.»
fact: The Golden Rule means: do to others what you would want them to do to you.
fact: A moral is the lesson a story teaches, as the Duchess says: «Everything's got a moral, if only you can find it.»
fact: Parents teach children to ride a bike, swim and cross the road safely.
exercise: «Jesus taught the Golden Rule: do to others what you would want them to do to you.» What does taught mean here? | Lost it on a journey | Wrote it on a wall | *Showed and explained it to people | Forgot it completely
exercise: «That will teach you to leave your bike outside!» What does it mean? | You must ride your bike to school | You will be given a new bike as a prize | You are very good at fixing bikes | *You have learned the hard way
exercise: In a story, what is a moral? | A kind of song the characters sing | *The lesson a story teaches | The last page of the book | A character who is very brave
test: «At the yearly check-up a dog gets a vaccine that teaches its body to fight dangerous illnesses.» What does teaches mean here? | Makes the dog sleepy | Gives the dog a bath | *Helps its body learn how to fight illness | Shows the dog how to fetch
test: Which sentence uses teach to mean giving lessons as a job? | Dad taught the dog to sit. | The mistake taught me to check twice. | Mum teaches me to swim every summer. | *Mum teaches maths at the local school.
exam: Which word is the past tense of teach? | teach | teaches | teaching | *taught
